From 0fcb253d719bf7869ec9df2a7a53bdede1c32772 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local <local@localhost>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 13:18:11 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 08/19] ROCm: gfx12 WMMA GEMV to 32 rows with two M tiles

bsz 4 x 8 verify rows (and the DFlash2 draft's 4 x 8-row block) are 32 rows
per linear, still past the 16-row WMMA kernel. M = 32 runs two 16-row M
tiles: each decoded trellis tile is staged through LDS once and its B
fragment feeds two v_wmma_f32_16x16x16_f16, one for rows 0-15 and one for
rows 16-31. The trellis is still read and decoded once per tile; only the
WMMA count and the A loads double. Accumulation stays fp32.

- Row tile 8 / 16 / 32 picked from size_m; the 8- and 16-row
  specializations compile to the same code as before (MT = 1).
- Every output element sees the same K order (warp chunk, U batch, WMMA) at
  every M, so a row's value does not depend on which row tile it ran in.
- At M = 32 the cross-wave reduction scratch (warps x 32 x 16 fp32)
  overlays the B staging slots after a block barrier. Stacked, the two
  reach 64 KB at 16 waves (the 17408-wide MLP down projection runs 16).
  Aliased, it is 32 KB.
- EXL3_GEMV_MAX_M defaults to 32 (clamp 1..32); 16 or 8 restore the
  earlier limits for A/B runs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
